From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:42:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: keep an idle external DCP powered by
 default

A T8132 external DCP with nothing attached powers its CPU, front-end
and system domains off after dcpext_idle_ms (5 s by default). On the
J604, the only board that names the power-down's PMC interface, that
happens about 6 s into every boot, and boots still stop there now and
then with no log until the watchdog resets the SoC. The power-down
unlinks the system domain's bus bridge with a single read-back and no
wait for the block to drain, and nothing describes how to wait.

Default dcpext_idle_ms to 0, so an idle external DCP stays powered
until a sleep powers the SoC down; the parameter still sets a delay.
A system sleep keeps its own power-down.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 6ac7736227..623a75e038 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -367,10 +367,11 @@ module_param(hdmi_idle_release, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(hdmi_idle_release,
 		 "T8132 HDMI: let the DP PHY and crossbar output go while the dcpext is idle (default: N; experimental)");
 
-static unsigned int dcpext_idle_ms = DCP_M4_EXT_IDLE_MS_DEFAULT;
+/* Off by default: the idle power-down is where some J604 boots still stop. */
+static unsigned int dcpext_idle_ms;
 module_param(dcpext_idle_ms, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(dcpext_idle_ms,
-		 "T8132: power an external display processor down after this many ms with nothing attached (0: never; 1000-600000; read at the next attach or detach)");
+		 "T8132: power an external display processor down after this many ms with nothing attached (default 0: never; 1000-600000; read at the next attach or detach)");
 
 module_param(show_notch, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(show_notch, "Use the full display height and show the notch (also when /chosen/asahi,show-notch is \"1\")");
-- 
